itadict - offline Italian dictionary

The dictionary data in data/ is derived from four sources.

it.wiktionary (Italian Wiktionary)
  Site: https://it.wiktionary.org/
  Extraction: https://kaikki.org/itwiktionary/Italiano/kaikki.org-dictionary-Italiano.jsonl
  Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Changes: fields pruned, glosses cleaned and shortened, headwords sharded,
  inflected forms moved to a separate index.
  27 pages flagged for copyright review are excluded; the list is in
  tools/data-exclusions.json.

en.wiktionary (English Wiktionary, Italian entries)
  Site: https://en.wiktionary.org/
  Extraction: https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Italian/kaikki.org-dictionary-Italian.jsonl
  Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Changes: only word, part of speech and the senses' glosses are kept. Three
  glosses per part of speech, shortened, and joined to the Italian entry.

Tatoeba Italian sentences
  Site: https://tatoeba.org/
  Export: https://downloads.tatoeba.org/exports/per_language/ita/ita_sentences.tsv.bz2
  Licence: CC BY 2.0 FR - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/
  Changes: sentence text is shortened. Tatoeba sentence ids are kept, so every
  example can be traced back to its author.

FrequencyWords Italian 50k list
  Author: Hermit Dave
  Export: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords/master/content/2018/it/it_50k.txt
  Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Changes: used only to rank lemmas into CEFR bands. No word list is shipped.

All four licences allow redistribution with attribution. This NOTICE must ship
with the data. Derived data stays under the same licences.
